// Title: User Added To Admin Group Via DseditGroup
// Sigma ID: 5d0fdb62-f225-42fb-8402-3dfe64da468a
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sohan G (D4rkCiph3r)
// Date: 2023-08-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, initial-access, privilege-escalation, stealth, T1078.003
// Description: Detects attempts to create and/or add an account to the admin group, thus granting admin
//   privileges.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/master/atomics/T1078.003/T1078.003.md#atomic-test-5---add-a-newexisting-user-to-the-admin-group-using-dseditgroup-utility---macos
//   - https://ss64.com/osx/dseditgroup.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_dseditgroup_add_to_admin_group.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/dseditgroup" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -o edit " and ProcessCommandLine contains " -a " and ProcessCommandLine contains " -t user" and ProcessCommandLine contains "admin")
